# name: test_dns_records_md_snapshot
  '''
  # DNS Records for dng.example.com

  > Auto-generated by dng-preflight.
  >
  > Publish these records **before** running `install.sh`. Recommended TTL is
  > 300 seconds while bringing the system up; raise to 3600 once stable.

  ## Base host

  | Type | Name | Value | TTL |
  |------|------|-------|-----|
  | A    | `dng.example.com` | `203.0.113.10` | 300 |


  ## Wildcard

  A wildcard record is required because the deployment uses a wildcard
  certificate (typical for RDP/SMB scope or multi-app deployments).

  | Type | Name | Value | TTL |
  |------|------|-------|-----|
  | A    | `*.example.com` | `203.0.113.10` | 300 |


  ## RDP/SMB subdomain delegation

  The RDP/SMB compose variant uses an extra DNS container that resolves
  external relay names to internal hosts. Delegate each external subdomain
  listed in `subdomains:` of `scripted-config.yaml` to the DNG host via NS.

  | Type | Name | Value | TTL |
  |------|------|-------|-----|
  | NS   | `<external_subdomain>` | `dng.example.com` | 3600 |


  ## Seed application hostnames

  These are pre-populated as stubs in `scripted-config.yaml`; fill in the
  real backend addresses there. The DNS records below cover the public-facing
  relay hostnames you'll choose:

  | Type | Name | Value | TTL |
  |------|------|-------|-----|
  | A    | `web-1.example.com` | `<DNG host public IP>` | 300 |
  | A    | `web-2.example.com` | `<DNG host public IP>` | 300 |
  | A    | `ssh-1.example.com` | `<DNG host public IP>` | 300 |
  | A    | `rdp-1.example.com` | `<DNG host public IP>` | 300 |


  ## Verification

  After publication, confirm propagation:

  ```bash
  dig @1.1.1.1 +short dng.example.com A
  dig @8.8.8.8 +short dng.example.com A
  ```

  Both should return the public IP of the DNG host within one TTL.

  '''
